Working agreements: implement ONLY this step (do not start other steps); follow existing conventions and _dev/loop-engineering/phases-plans/contracts.md; read CLAUDE.md at the repo root before touching code. Verification commands — 'python' and 'pytest' are NOT on PATH on this machine, always use the venv interpreter: from the repo root run 'venv/Scripts/python.exe -m pytest tests/ -q', then from frontend/ run 'npm run test' and 'npm run build'. Get all three green BEFORE committing; finish with exactly one commit whose subject contains 'step 11.1'. Do not push."
The commit landed cleanly: `5f81306c feat(providers): step 11.1 - Generalize the registry into a domain hub` — 13 files changed, 816 insertions, 273 deletions, with `domains.py`, `hub.py`, and `test_provider_hub.py` added. Working tree is clean.

Step 11.1's Done-when conditions are all met:

| Requirement | Evidence |
|---|---|
| All five domains register with the hub | `hub.domains()` → `['script', 'scene_blueprint', 'tts', 'storyboard', 'animator']`; startup logs each with its count |
| Existing TTS/Storyboard/Animator imports still work | `CompatibilityFacadeTests` asserts `studio.tts.providers.registry is hub.registry('tts')` and that all three `init_<domain>_registry` remain callable |
| Duplicate domains/providers fail deterministically | `test_duplicate_id_keeps_the_incumbent`, `test_wrong_domain_registration_is_refused`, `test_unknown_domain_fails_deterministically` |
| Discovery order is stable | `test_discovery_order_is_sorted_not_filesystem_order` |
| Broken provider can't hide healthy ones or stop startup | `test_broken_providers_are_excluded_individually` (6 distinct failure modes alongside one healthy provider), `test_only_broken_providers_still_completes_discovery` |

One caveat worth flagging for 11.2: the hub currently discovers lazily on `get`/`list`/`catalog`, and discovery still mutates the live registry dict rather than publishing an atomic snapshot. That's D21 and is already assigned to 11.2 — but until it lands, a lookup racing a first-time discovery in a request thread can observe a partially populated domain. In practice `init_providers()` at startup discovers everything before the server serves, so the window doesn't open in the running app.

